*.pyc
# resource-monitor.sh output: lands in the repo root whenever an orchestrator
# runs without --log-dir (its --out-dir default is REPO_ROOT)
resources-*.csv
resources-*.summary.txt
*.deb
windows/downloads/*
# Keep the README so a fresh clone has the directory: Dockerfile.nvidia does an
# unconditional `COPY downloads C:\temp\downloads` that FAILS when the (otherwise
# fully gitignored) directory is absent from the build context.
!windows/downloads/README.md
linux/llm-stack/ollama-binary.tar.zst
linux/llm-stack/.env
linux/llm-stack/benchmark_results/
linux/llm-stack/benchmark-viewer/dist/
linux/llm-stack/benchmark-viewer/node_modules/
linux/nextcloud-aio/.env
.claude/*
# ...except the safety gate. A guard that only exists on one machine is not a
# guard: a fresh clone, or a `git clean -xdf`, would silently disarm it
# (2026-08-21 host wipe). settings.local.json stays ignored - it is personal.
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
.claude/hooks/*
!.claude/hooks/guard-destructive-deletes.ps1

# Throwaway litert-lm fast-rebuild harness (overlays the build script onto a local
# windows-media-litert base image to re-iterate only litert-lm; dev-only, not reproducible in CI)
.cxxtest.Dockerfile

# Qualcomm AI Engine Direct (QAIRT/QNN) SDK zip, staged by hand for the ORT QNN EP
# (Windows: #121; Linux ARM64: backlog QNN-LINUX). Login-gated + EULA-bound, never
# committed. Only the README rides along on each lane.
windows/qnn-sdk/*
!windows/qnn-sdk/README.md
linux/qnn-sdk/*
!linux/qnn-sdk/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch and one-shot helpers — never committed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ad-hoc drivers (a refactor script, a probe, a generated fragment) land in the
# repo ROOT because that is where a `uv run` / `bash` invocation resolves
# relative paths — and that is exactly where `git add -A` sweeps them into a
# commit. NO tracked file at the root is a script, so root-level scripts are
# ignored outright; put anything else throwaway under .scratch/.
#
# Safe against every gate, checked 2026-08-25: lint-shell.sh and lint-python.sh
# both discover from explicit directory allowlists (linux/scripts, docs/scripts,
# linux/llm-stack, linux/webserver) that exclude the root and .scratch/, and
# crlf-guard reads `git ls-files`, so it never sees an ignored file. No
# Dockerfile COPYs a root-level script either — the mirrored entries in
# .dockerignore keep a stray one out of the build context, where it would
# otherwise change the root context ~9 builds upload per full run.
#
# If a helper earns a SECOND use it is not scratch any more: move it to
# linux/scripts/ or docs/scripts/, give it a header and a test, and commit it
# there. Committing one deliberately is still `git add -f <file>`.
/.scratch/
/*.py
/*.sh
/*.ps1
/*.psm1
/*.tmp
/*.bak
